# Skills Index

`skills/SKILLS.txt` is a generated table: one row per `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`
with name (version), objective and the summarized context in which the skill
is used. Source of every cell is the frontmatter (`name`, `description`,
`metadata.version`). Never edit `SKILLS.txt` by hand.

- After creating, changing or deleting any `SKILL.md`, run
  `python3 skills/scripts/skills-index.py` and commit `skills/SKILLS.txt`
  together with the skill.
- `python3 skills/scripts/skills-index.py --check` exits 1 when the index is
  stale. Run it before declaring a skill change done.
- The generator takes the first sentence of `description` as the objective
  and the text from "Use when" / "Use quando" / "Triggers" as the context.
  Write descriptions in that shape; bump `metadata.version` on every change.
- `skills/SKILLS.md` is the hand-written Portuguese companion, grouped by
  area. It is not generated: when a skill is created, changed or removed,
  update its row (and the total in the header) in the same commit.
- Claude Code: the `PostToolUse` hook in `.claude/settings.json` regenerates
  the index after each edit of a `SKILL.md`. Other tools: run the command.
